.TH REMOTERIG-CLIENT 1 "September 2026" "RemoteRig 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remoterig\-client \- operate a remote amateur radio transceiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remoterig\-client
.RI [ --list-audio ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to a RemoteRig server and gives the operator the rig's audio, its PTT
and, when the rig supports CAT, its frequency, mode, VFO and band selection.
.PP
Hold the transmit button or the space bar to talk. Click the frequency display
to type one: megahertz, kilohertz or hertz are all accepted.
.PP
A rigctld interface can be published on 127.0.0.1:4532 so that WSJT\-X, fldigi
or VARA drive the remote rig as if it were local.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-audio
Print every audio interface and device PortAudio can see, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/F4JTV/RemoteRigClient.conf
Settings: host, ports, audio devices, microphone shaping, theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR remoterig-server (1),
.BR wsjtx (1)
